@@ -0,0 +1,347 @@
+# v4.1: complete the failed v4 fits without changing the problem
+
+V4.1 addresses the observed memory exits, nuisance-profile timeouts and failed
+fits. Its completion requires successful full native orbit estimation and the
+unchanged numerical equivalence gates. Passing component tests, avoiding
+retries or completing one fixed-parameter propagation does not establish that
+the release works.
+
+Development, builds, inputs and outputs are separate from the frozen v4
+campaign. That campaign keeps its pinned executables, source, execution order,
+resource limits and results. V4.1 results must never fill its failed or missing
+slots. The original 150-attempt v3.1 deliverable also remains separately
+attributed. Existing public commands, validation rules and compatibility
+defaults remain in force; adding candidate input tools does not enable a new
+estimator by default.
+
+## Measured starting point
+
+The v4 failure investigation is published in
+`validation/v4-fit-reliability/candidate02/report.json`. It explicitly has no
+whole-fit, accepted-covariance, speedup or release authority.
+
+* The 48-hour density cases retained full position and velocity design arrays
+  in GNSS processing. A nuisance child inherited resident arrays; the unchanged
+  process-tree RSS rule counted the parent and child and stopped the fit.
+* The 72-hour density evaluator allocated approximately 10 GiB for its full
+  designs before reaching the nuisance profile. The separate blocked evaluator
+  completed that stage within the memory limit, but did not establish a full
+  nonlinear fit or solve the retained GNSS design problem.
+* The archived 72-hour pulse profiles failed their mandatory zero-update replay
+  and every ordinary child trial reached its 300-second limit. The historical
+  zero replay did not retain its underlying error. These records do not prove
+  objective/cache corruption. Clearer diagnostics and fail-fast rejection do
+  not make the first child complete.
+* Initial, repeated and tighter-closure cold nuisance profiles consumed the
+  time allowance on shorter cases. The independently tested warm-start work
+  establishes fixed-trajectory profile checks, not complete fits. Any v4.1
+  integration must retain its cold-source, cold-repeat and changed-trajectory
+  cold-target checks.
+
+The candidate06 warm-start publication is at the external artifact
+`/mnt/d/orbit-nuisance-warmstarts/publication/candidate06-profiles03/summary.json`.
+Its 27 completed profiles and 15 checks explicitly grant no accepted orbit
+covariance or whole-fit convergence claim. This historical absolute path is an
+evidence locator, not a portable dependency or a current validation result.
+
+## Preserved physical and statistical model
+
+The initial physical state, full accumulated inertial pulses in native µm/s,
+post-pulse velocity convention, and 60-second linearly interpolated log-density
+knots remain unchanged. There is one stationary OU initial prior and each OU
+transition once. Computational storage or segment boundaries introduce no
+additional priors, continuity noise, ambiguity resets or physical restarts.
+
+Every nonlinear trial propagates the complete chronological physical history,
+refits float GNSS nuisance parameters and measures the direct original-row
+objective including eliminated residual energy. Observations, weights,
+ambiguity arcs, gauges, force models, preprocessing, initialization and selected
+hyperparameters stay fixed. Rejected trials cannot change accepted parameters,
+receiver state, caches or force history. Warm starts supply starting coordinates
+only and may not supply information or waive strict stationarity.
+
+Memory fixes must retain the exact discrete tangent, interpolation stencils,
+parameter units, rank certificate and nuisance-marginalized uncertainty.
+Changing RSS accounting to PSS, increasing limits, removing covariance queries,
+discarding coefficients, adding ridge priors or accepting numerical-floor
+progress as convergence is not a fix for these requirements.
+
+## Acceptance ledger
+
+Every result below must bind the actual candidate source, native binary,
+segmented solver, runtime dependencies, original inputs and execution receipt.
+Independent audit must inspect those outputs, not just summary pass flags.
+
+| Requirement | Evidence needed for completion |
+|---|---|
+| Reference preservation | The unchanged 106 native tests and 51 correction regressions, with no failures or skips; all four propagation/measurement refinements; both objective/prior checks; both distinct original nuisance-failure replays. |
+| Original input identity | All 14 prescribed original artifact hashes in `segmented.validation_reference`, protected test/script bytes, complete native data membership and exact original replay physical inputs. |
+| Propagation/interpolation refinement | Both synthetic methods, flight window and eccentric 24-hour case; predicted measurements change by less than 1% of their assumed noise, with unchanged component position limits. |
+| Original objective and full priors | Nonzero full pulse and OU penalties. Relative directional error plus measured resolution at most `1e-4` at two consecutive scales; unchanged half-scale schedule, nine-scale maximum and physical-repeat allowance. |
+| Strict nuisance replay | Two consecutive undamped updates below `1e-8 m`, exact zero transactions, fixed support/weights and no numerical-floor substitution. |
+| Discrete tangent | Lifted true residual below `2e-12`, physical boundaries, shifted cuts, interpolation halos, precise times, pulse conversion and density continuity. |
+| Small native linearization | Same original weighted rows compared against dense QR and independent GTSAM; MAP discrepancy below `1e-7` posterior SD and covariance relative error below `1e-8`, including zero and nonzero LM damping. |
+| Structural correctness | Exact/near rank deficiencies, missing constraints, globally resolved local deficiencies, disconnected ambiguities, unit/row/block invariance, full nonzero priors, nuisance elimination and selected cross-covariance. |
+| Storage and process correctness | Exact values/strides/shapes and interpolation behavior; shared-storage lifetime and fork tests; explicit I/O and allocation failures; complete owned-process cleanup; measured scratch storage and process-tree RSS. |
+| Timeout regression | Exact archived 72-hour pulse profiles clear the unchanged 300-second child deadline, then full original-case fits finish under the unchanged fit limits. Avoided futile retries alone do not satisfy this gate. |
+| Memory regression | Exact 48-hour density GNSS profiles and 72-hour density full fits remain within 8 GiB process-tree RSS, including child processes, fresh final linearization and covariance recovery. |
+| Nonlinear convergence | Fresh undamped maximum position correction below `30 µm`, density below `1e-4` or pulse below `1e-8 m/s`, normalized scaled gradient below `1e-8`, and strict nuisance convergence. Small damped steps and exhausted budgets cannot pass. |
+| Rank and covariance | Original-coordinate, undamped dense QR/SVD certificate with original stochastic row/column counts. Singular values at or below `epsilon * max(m,n) * sigma_max` are deficient; values through ten times that limit are unresolved. Neither receives accepted covariance. Final covariance is fresh, undamped and nuisance marginalized. |
+| Full native equivalence | Matching inputs/support/weights; position difference below `30 µm`, unchanged density/pulse tolerances, predictions below 1% noise, and objective agreement within measured numerical floors. Grid, observation, dynamic and cross-segment covariance normalized errors below `1e-6`. |
+| Mandatory long case | Strict successful 72-hour 500 km disturbed/daily-blackout fits for both pulse and density methods, with the required segmented profile. |
+| Bounded flight | Exact April 24 normal/blackout inputs for both methods across dense, 1-hour and 4-hour profiles: 12 fits and eight successful equivalence comparisons. |
+| Complete results | A separate v4.1 report covering every planned attempt and failure, with no dense-success/segmented-failure regression, independent audit and the preserved original campaign reports. |
+
+The existing native gate registry is
+`src/orbit_poc/segmented/validation.py`; release-level checks are in
+`src/orbit_poc/segmented/report.py`. The diagnostic nuisance runner can record
+audited numerical-floor progress, but the release parser requires strict
+convergence and two strict final undamped updates. Its process exit code alone
+cannot pass this gate.
+
+The fixed original matrix contains 68 attempts: 24 synthetic 24-hour, 16
+synthetic 48-hour, 16 synthetic 72-hour and 12 flight. A new v4.1 execution must
+be frozen separately. Shared seeds, nested durations and profile variants are
+not independent scientific trials. Do not replace a failed case with a shorter,
+better conditioned or otherwise easier one. Report all successful paired
+equivalence results and every unavailable comparison.
+
+Retain one numerical thread, 8 GiB process-tree RSS, 32 accepted iterations,
+96 total trials and two hours per fit. Protect production work and the frozen
+campaign using current-host admission and exact owned-process cleanup. A host
+or old lock file is not evidence that a CPU is currently free.
+
+## Exact regression input preparation
+
+The historical frozen manifest is captured locally at
+`/mnt/d/orbit-segmented-v4/control/preparation07-terminal01/run/manifest.json`,
+SHA256 `4877f929be8a9eda5d58ff6b4eb0e0fc8b84ea16934a6fbe63fa5a18418fa5c6`.
+Its internal manifest hash is
+`63f3010564c6da76c0f92a007ed1fbe057d610d44cccb6b5e4f509afafbf2251`.
+`cases[*].fit_request` contains prepared case-request subsets, and the prepared
+catalog is pinned separately. These subsets are not the executable per-profile
+jobs. The actual job is archived at
+`attempts/<attempt_id>/request.json`; `protocol.attempt_job` derives it from the
+frozen manifest and plan, adding the selected runtime, numerical controls,
+profile and job hash. Verify that complete reconstruction against the captured
+execution request before adapting a regression. A preparation-request byte hash
+must not be applied to its distinct derived execution-request file.
+
+The external audit
+`/home/emper/orbit-v4.1/evidence/request-attribution01.json` reconstructs both
+initial regression execution requests exactly. Their captured SHA256 values are
+`95afc9661d9054a701287d6f8886b29789e3fb382201fe6670fcc7228ee7bf72`
+for the 72-hour pulse case and
+`2af6dcabcb82e7cc70bc718b020da2f927a8aa567d6e5a01d0cf7dc1bf85aae6`
+for the 48-hour density case. The initial capture mistakes, which compared each
+execution request with its preparation-file hash, remain recorded as failures;
+the attribution audit does not overwrite them. These are historical locators
+and hashes, not a claim that every external file is currently present on a new
+host.
+
+The first exact regressions are
+`leo500-quiet-normal-groops_pulses-72h--dense_corrected` and
+`leo500-quiet-normal-groops_log_drag_ou-48h--dense_corrected`.
+Keep two distinct input objects for each:
+
+1. The original per-profile executable job, its prepared-case request, nominal
+   initialization and all retained observations/products.
+2. The archived failed `point-001-initial/profile.xml`, already closed
+   variational archive, full physical parameters and reachable GNSS inputs.
+
+A fixed-point replay diagnoses the failing stage. It cannot replace a fit from
+the original starting state. The later disturbed/blackout cases remain required.
+Flight retains its historical density settings, `tau=7200 s`, `sigma_g=0.3`;
+fresh synthetic density keeps `tau=1800 s`, `sigma_g=0.1`. Pulse settings remain
+1200 seconds and `1e-4 m/s`.
+
+`scripts/stage_v41_regressions.py` stages **already captured local files**:
+
+```sh
+python scripts/stage_v41_regressions.py plan --inventory /absolute/new-inventory.json
+python scripts/stage_v41_regressions.py stage --inventory /absolute/new-inventory.json
+```
+
+The tool performs no SSH, downloads, native work, process cleanup or benchmark
+mutation. `plan` validates and prints a plan without creating the destination;
+incomplete execution inputs return a nonzero status. `stage` requires a new
+destination and a complete declared input set. A failed partial copy is retained
+with `failure.json`; there is no overwrite/resume/delete option.
+
+Its independently bounded JSON inventory has this form:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": "orbit-poc-v41-regression-staging-v1",
+  "destination": "/absolute/new-attempt-inputs",
+  "path_prefixes": ["/original/frozen/input/root"],
+  "files": [
+    {
+      "original_path": "/original/frozen/input/root/observations.dat",
+      "source_path": "/already/captured/observations.dat",
+      "sha256": "the_verified_64_character_lowercase_digest",
+      "bytes": 123,
+      "kind": "data"
+    }
+  ],
+  "generated_paths": [],
+  "xml_templates": {}
+}
+```
+
+The example digest is a placeholder, deliberately not a runnable inventory.
+Allowed kinds are `data`, `xml`, `preparation` and `request`. Prefixes must be
+nonoverlapping absolute original roots. Optional `generated_paths` explicitly
+names future propagation outputs; it cannot hide a missing captured input.
+Optional `xml_templates` maps a complete original GROOPS path expression such
+as a `{prn}` filename to its explicitly captured concrete members. The stager
+does not guess satellite or date coverage.
+
+Sources must be regular files without symlink ancestors. Unknown options,
+duplicate JSON keys, unsafe paths, mismatched hashes, input drift, undeclared
+wildcard-visible native files and evaluation truth are rejected. Original data
+bytes remain intact. XML is rewritten only at complete path text nodes, and its
+inverse mapping must reproduce the original bytes. Original structured files
+are archived separately. Every JSON path/hash/length edit has an inverse journal
+that reconstructs the original object; copied artifact references receive the
+actual staged hash and length. Native directory inventory and blind GNSS-only
+preparation metadata are checked.
+
+Uncopied historical product/source/boundary provenance retains its original
+paths and hashes. Runtime/backend identities remain historical. The resulting
+manifest therefore says `prepared_inputs_only` and `launch_ready=false`, even
+after successful staging. A separate reviewed execution freeze must bind the
+candidate executable, dependencies, source, complete runtime input closure,
+observation support, thresholds and current-host admission. Never launch a
+staged request simply because the copy succeeded.
+
+## Separate candidate build
+
+Build from a fresh pinned upstream checkout and a separate output directory:
+
+```sh
+python scripts/build_groops.py \
+  --numerics --segmented --wide-tangent-candidate \
+  --nuisance-performance --variational-memory-candidate --reliability-v41 \
+  --source-dir /absolute/new-v41-native-source \
+  --build-dir /absolute/new-v41-native-build \
+  --prefix /absolute/pinned-compiler-and-dependencies --jobs 1
+```
+
+The upstream revision remains
+`7e1bd6dc8bf2fb1c9180f2f9366efa7e7b4477ee`. `--reliability-v41` requires all
+five preceding numerical/profile flags; it installs the separate nuisance and
+design-storage overlays after their prerequisites. The build command does not
+activate their runtime behavior or establish any acceptance gate.
+
+Runtime defaults remain `ORBIT_POC_NUISANCE_FIXED_DYNAMICS=0` and
+`ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_STORAGE=memory`. A separately frozen candidate run may
+select `1` and `disk`, respectively; disk mode also requires its explicitly
+owned `ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_SCRATCH` directory. Record every selected control
+with source, compiler, executable, complete dependency hashes and resource
+limits before execution. Keep original benchmark runtimes untouched.
+
+Independent path counterexamples in `tests/test_v41_build_paths.py` exposed
+source-freeze weaknesses involving symlink substitutions with identical bytes
+and dangling profile receipts. The builder now rejects these paths before any
+installer runs. Preserve the original failed checks separately from the passing
+checks of the corrected build controls. A subsequently hardened build must have
+its own source, build and executable identity; the control correction does not
+retroactively change candidate01's build evidence.
+
+## Initial native profile equivalence experiment
+
+`scripts/run_v41_profile_pairs.py` provides separate `prepare` and `run` commands
+for the explicitly pinned local candidate01 experiment. Its site-specific
+candidate paths identify archived inputs; they are not a replacement public
+configuration interface. `prepare` does not launch native work. It requires a
+new output directory, copies only output-remapped XML profiles, verifies exact
+source inputs, creates owned scratch directories, and freezes the runtime,
+archived compiled installer snapshot, checker dependencies and execution order.
+`run --freeze /absolute/attempt/freeze.json` verifies that inventory again and
+refuses existing execution artifacts; any interrupted attempt remains intact.
+
+The four groups are pulse/density crossed with native epoch accumulation off/on.
+Each group has three treatments: in-memory designs with fixed-dynamics skipping
+off, in-memory designs with fixed-dynamics skipping on, and 64-epoch disk blocks
+with fixed-dynamics skipping on. All twelve runs keep interpolation caching and
+cost-only child designs enabled, with unchanged cold checks and convergence
+thresholds. The frozen order balances both temporal orders of each treatment
+pair across the four groups. CPU0, one numerical thread, an 8 GiB process-tree
+limit and a 7,200-second deadline remain fixed; admission is a cooperative
+current-host check, not a claim of exclusive CPU reservation.
+
+`scripts/check_v41_profile_pair.py` checks eight declared pairs using the existing
+scientific artifact comparison. It removes only the three already excluded
+trial-resource fields; all remaining scientific data must match exactly.
+Separate measured counter sidecars must prove the actual fixed-dynamics and
+disk treatments, and their byte hashes are retained and rechecked. All arms
+truthfully declare cost-only designs enabled; no receipt is rewritten to imitate
+the older cost-off/cost-on experiment. Strict nuisance convergence is required
+for a passing pair. Numerical-floor-limited progress remains a failed gate.
+These are fixed-trajectory profile checks: even eight successful pairs cannot
+authorize covariance, establish complete orbit-fit convergence or close any of
+the whole-fit acceptance requirements above.
+
+## Separate whole-fit regression controls
+
+`scripts/run_v41_wholefit_regressions.py prepare --spec /absolute/spec.json`
+freezes the exact 72-hour quiet/normal 500 km pulse failure and 48-hour
+quiet/normal 500 km density failure as two new, outcome-selected experiments.
+The strict `orbit-poc-v41-wholefit-spec-v1` object requires `experiment_id`
+(starting with `v41-`), a new absolute `output_dir`, `source_root`, and
+`{path, sha256}` pins for `staging_manifest`, `staging_plan`, `staging_audit`,
+`build_result` and `python`. Unknown options are rejected. Preparation copies
+runtime Python sources, templates, configurations and lockfiles into a separate
+read-only snapshot. Native compiled source and feature receipts are bound
+separately through the completed build result. NumPy, SciPy, psutil and their
+bundled libraries are fingerprinted; this does not certify a complete Python
+standard-library or operating-system dependency closure.
+
+Only the original **executable attempt** requests may supply these cases.
+Prepared-case request subsets are insufficient. Staging must reproduce the
+original request under its inverse path mapping. The new requests preserve all
+physical inputs, observations, initialization, weights, priors, hyperparameters,
+mask, numerical controls and `dense_corrected` profile. They receive distinct
+experiment, protocol, source, input and job identities and bind the selected
+candidate executable. These results never overwrite frozen campaign attempts.
+
+The treatment explicitly selects interpolation caching, cost-only child designs,
+fixed-dynamics nuisance updates and performance counters, with 64-epoch GNSS
+disk blocks and 64-epoch variational closure blocks. Cold `V4Model` trajectory
+propagation and nuisance checks remain active. Fail-fast replay is enabled:
+a failed mandatory zero replay ends the invalid fit instead of initiating more
+futile trials. Its original 300-second child deadline, correctness thresholds
+and acceptance criteria remain unchanged; early failure is not a successful fix.
+CPU0, one numerical thread, the 8 GiB process-tree limit and 7,200-second fit
+limit remain fixed. Admission also requires 16 GiB available host memory and
+32 GiB free output space; it is a cooperative host check, not an exclusive
+reservation.
+
+Preparation never launches a fit. An explicit
+`run --freeze /absolute/experiment/freeze.json` rechecks all identities, rejects
+existing execution output, and supervises one fit at a time with owned-process
+cleanup. `report --freeze /absolute/experiment/freeze.json --output
+/absolute/new-report` includes both planned attempts even when they are missing,
+interrupted, failed or resource-limited. Actual native logs, control receipts,
+fixed-dynamics counters and disk-storage evidence remain attributable to their
+bytes. Strict final nuisance convergence, undamped full-rank linearization,
+optimizer confirmation and fresh covariance gates are required for a full-fit
+pass. Floor-limited progress cannot authorize covariance. Two successful
+regressions do not satisfy the wider reference, segmented, flight, 72-hour
+**disturbed/blackout** or complete 68-attempt release requirements.
+
+## Reporting and remaining physical limitations
+
+Publish provenance, every interruption/failure, strict convergence and rank,
+actual objective, prediction/covariance differences, rejected trials,
+propagation counts, retained separator/factor sizes, scratch bytes, peak memory
+and time by stage. Dense rank-certification costs remain included in totals and
+visible separately. Mixed single timings do not establish a repeatable speedup.
+
+Flight remains `flight_gravity_drag_v1`, with omitted thermal-history
+sensitivities, gradients of forces other than gravity and drag, and atmospheric
+event-time derivatives. Flight numerical equivalence validates that existing
+approximation, not a complete physical uncertainty model. The inferred quantity
+remains an effective drag correction; independent density recovery and
+accuracy-superiority claims are outside these numerical fixes.
