+# Conditional nuisance QR candidate03
+
+This separate source candidate is uncompiled and has no native validation or
+release authority. It starts from the current v4.1 core copied into
+`conditional-qr03/source`; the running candidate02 replay and its sources are
+unchanged. `source-copy.json` records the copied bytes.
+
+The measured density replay's first factor has 4,680 retained columns: 2,887
+physical and 1,793 nuisance. Its first parent row build took about 665 seconds;
+dynamic observation design accounted for about 73 seconds. These are measurements
+of candidate02, not evidence of candidate03 speed or convergence.
+
+`ORBIT_POC_NUISANCE_CONDITIONAL_QR=1` selects compact retained nuisance QR only
+inside `profile_step`. The default remains zero. All original observation designs,
+finite-value checks, group STEC QR, clock/VTEC elimination, constraints and precise
+residual ledgers remain in place. Physical-prior rows still enter the spool with
+their residuals and zero selected nuisance coefficients. Retained nuisance indices
+keep their original order; recovered corrections are scattered into a complete
+native vector with exact physical zeros. This version does not omit dynamic
+observation design construction.
+
+The compact factor has a conditional schema and `.conditional_factor.json`
+suffix. It cannot enter an unrestricted physical solve, damped solve, full
+diagnostic export or covariance query. Conditional rows are not exported as full
+segmented graph rows. Full parameter names remain recorded; excluded physical
+entries explicitly have an unscaled placeholder in their conditional inventory.
+
+Two consecutive inner influences below the unchanged `1e-8 m` threshold still
+trigger a fresh full original-coordinate, undamped QR and rank certificate. For
+the conditional candidate, `linearize_confirm` also recovers the full system's
+nuisance correction and evaluates zero and unit updates in isolated children.
+The zero replay must be exact, and the unit correction's full native influence
+must be below the same threshold. Disagreement is a failure. The parent state is
+never updated by confirmation. The original 300-second child deadline remains.
+Floor-limited progress cannot become strict convergence or authorize covariance.
+The backend rejects missing, conditional or incomplete full-factor certificates.
+
+The final overlay installer runs after the existing v4.1 overlays and before the
+new build profile is sealed. It refuses an already sealed source tree, validates
+all anchors before writing, and verifies exact regular-file receipt membership on
+reentry. The original source/build tree must not be reused for candidate03.
+
+Pure Python tests cover original-row algebra, coupled local/group recovery,
+noncontiguous mappings, nonzero fixed physical prior costs, empty retained
+nuisances, deficient and unresolved rank, full confirmation gates, installer
+identity and build admission. These tests do not validate compiled C++.
+
+`tests/test_conditional_nuisance_native.py` is a pending suite requiring an explicit
+`ORBIT_POC_V41_CONDITIONAL_NATIVE` binary. It compares compact and full-constrained
+native corrections against original-row QR and GTSAM 4.2 QR, tests authority
+guards and empty nuisance sets, and injects an EFBIG spool-write failure. The
+original native test files remain unchanged. Full GNSS pulse/density off/on
+profiles, cold checks, covariance, rejection-state behavior and the exact large
+cases remain required under the unchanged limits. No speedup can be inferred from
+the smaller factor dimensions alone.
+
+Spool transfer diagnostics now retain attempted/transferred element counts,
+immediately captured errno, stream status and the selected directory. Flush and
+seek failures are checked explicitly. The earlier candidate02 pulse error did
+not record errno and therefore is not certified as ENOSPC by this change.
